<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mauren</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mauren is a municipality in the Unterland of Liechtenstein, near the Austrian border. A farming village for most of its history, it belonged to the Lordship of Schellenberg, which the princes of Liechtenstein bought in 1699 and united with the County of Vaduz in 1719 to form the Principality of Liechtenstein.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mauren.jpg" alt="Mauren" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Plutowiki · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mauren_mit_Alpstein.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
